│ ╭────────────────────────────────── Remote access ───────────────────────────────────╮ │
│ │ Paste one of these into a terminal on your computer.                               │ │
│ │                                                                                    │ │
│ │ ▸ From anywhere, through borg cloud: run on your computer                          │ │
│ │     borg pair 'borg://relay.example.com/ababababababababababababababababababababab │ │
│ │     ababababababababababab#cdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcdcd'                       │ │
│ │     The link works once, for ten minutes. Approve the computer here when it asks.  │ │
│ │     Relay: wss://relay.example.com                                                 │ │
│ │                                                                                    │ │
│ │   Start Claude Code connected to this borg:                                        │ │
│ │     claude --mcp-config '{"mcpServers":{"borg-web1":{"command":"ssh","args":["-o", │ │
│ │     "BatchMode=yes","deploy@203.0.113.9","/home/deploy/.local/bin/borg mcp"]}}}'   │ │
│ │                                                                                    │ │
│ │   Or keep it in Claude Code for every session:                                     │ │
│ │     claude mcp add borg-web1 -- ssh -o BatchMode=yes deploy@203.0.113.9 '/home/dep │ │
│ │     loy/.local/bin/borg mcp'                                                       │ │
│ │                                                                                    │ │
│ │ Your computer reaches this server as: deploy@203.0.113.9                           │ │
│ │ SSH has to log in without a password prompt: a key, or an SSH agent.               │ │
│ │ Paired: me@laptop · F8 forgets them                                                │ │
│ ╰──────────── Tab picks · Enter copies · F3 shows it plain · Esc closes ─────────────╯ │
│                                           ││                                           │
